    "content": "Asian stock markets experienced a sharp decline, plunging deep into the red as global oil prices surged to $108 per barrel. Investors expressed growing concern over the economic impact of soaring energy costs, which threaten to fuel inflation and disrupt supply chains across the region. Major indices reacted negatively to the developments, reflecting widespread market anxiety amid the ongoing commodities rally.",
